{"step_index":2703,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:49:51Z","thinking":"The \"applyReviews\" function is triggered after the user reviews data in Excel and indicates whether the data is compliant or non-compliant. The primary function appears to communicate the review results to another component, potentially a backend or another part of the system. A preliminary check verifies that a process identifier exists.\n\n\nThe `applyReviews` function in the backend updates the target and \"not found\" sheets but neglects to modify the summary sheet, explaining the discrepancy. The returned data lacks a \"failed\" key and \"new_stats\" preventing the frontend from updating statistics or showing failures, confirming why the displayed results are stale. This omission directly results in the incorrect success message and the persistence of old stats on the app's results screen until the page is reloaded.\n\n\nThe backend's `apply_reviews` function must update the \"ملخص\" (summary) sheet within the Excel workbook; currently, it only modifies other sheets. Investigating the Excel writer's logic, specifically the structure of the \"ملخص\" sheet reveals that it contains header rows, total counts, matched items, unmatched items, items needing review, and details for each warehouse. Correcting the backend requires updating this sheet.\n\n\nExcel formulas can be incorporated into the summary sheet generation, or direct cell updates, or both. Using `COUNTA` to count rows, while accounting for header rows and potential empty ranges, appears to be the most robust approach to counting rows dynamically in the summary sheet. `apply_reviews` loads and saves the workbook so it can directly update the summary sheet with formula-based counts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html","ContentOffset":0,"EndLine":2120,"StartLine":2070,"toolAction":"Viewing loadResults in index.html","toolSummary":"View loadResults function"}}]}
